Package: PhysioHDEMG
Title: High-Density Surface EMG Motor-Unit Decomposition for the Physio Ecosystem
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Yusuke",
           family = "Matsui",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "mail.to.matsui@gmail.com")
Description: Decomposition of high-density surface electromyography
    (HD-sEMG) electrode-grid recordings into constituent motor-unit
    discharge patterns by convolutive blind source separation (extension,
    whitening and a fixed-point contrast maximisation with
    convolution-kernel-compensation refinement), following Holobar & Zazula
    (2007) and Negro et al. (2016). Provides motor-unit pulse trains,
    firing statistics (discharge rate, recruitment / derecruitment,
    pulse-to-noise ratio and silhouette quality), spatial motor-unit
    action-potential maps over the electrode grid, and a ground-truth
    HD-sEMG simulator for validation.
Depends:
    R (>= 4.2)
Imports:
    stats,
    utils
Suggests:
    PhysioCore,
    S4Vectors,
    SummarizedExperiment,
    testthat (>= 3.2.0)
